amdgpu: disable output bit-depth reduction dithering (truncate + spatial + temporal/FRC)

Force resource_build_bit_depth_reduction_params() to return immediately with
an all-zero bit_depth_reduction_params. That is bit-for-bit identical to the
driver's own DITHER_OPTION_DISABLE code path, so no truncation, no spatial
dither and no temporal dither (frame random / frame modulation, i.e. FRC) is
ever programmed into the FMT block of the OPP. Motivation: temporal dithering
(FRC) causes eye strain / nausea.

Generated against Ubuntu linux-source 7.0.0-38.38 (RDNA2 / Navi 22 tested).
rebuild.sh falls back to an anchor-based insertion if it does not apply.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c
@@ -5040,6 +5040,15 @@
 
 	memset(fmt_bit_depth, 0, sizeof(*fmt_bit_depth));
 
+	/*
+	 * LOCAL PATCH: disable all output bit-depth reduction, i.e.
+	 * truncation + spatial dithering + temporal dithering (FRC).
+	 * Returning here with fmt_bit_depth left all-zero is identical to
+	 * the driver's built-in DITHER_OPTION_DISABLE path just below.
+	 * Reason: temporal dithering causes eye strain / nausea.
+	 */
+	return;
+
 	if (option == DITHER_OPTION_DEFAULT) {
 		switch (stream->timing.display_color_depth) {
 		case COLOR_DEPTH_666:
